---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
const faqs = [
  ['How much does Booke AI cost compared with Botkeeper?', 'Booke AI Business is $129 per business per month; firm and white-label plans are by quote. Botkeeper Infinite licenses run from $149 per month (1 to 4 clients) down to $59 per month (25 or more), lower on annual billing.'],
  ['Does Booke AI work inside QuickBooks Online and Xero?', 'Yes. Booke AI works inside existing QuickBooks Online and Xero files, so client books stay where they are.'],
  ['Is Botkeeper only software, or does it include bookkeepers?', 'Botkeeper is a firm software platform (AI categorization, bank recs, Close Tracker, Activity Hub). Human bookkeeping services are an optional extra on top.'],
  ['Which is cheaper for a firm with many clients?', 'Botkeeper volume tiers drop to $59 per client per month at 25 or more licenses, below Booke AI’s $129 per business list price. For a few clients, Booke AI’s published price is simpler.'],
];
const faqLd = JSON.stringify({
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(([q, a]) => ({ '@type': 'Question', name: q, acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: a } })),
});
---
<Base
  title="Booke AI vs Botkeeper for bookkeeping firms — categorization compared"
  description="Side-by-side: Booke AI and Botkeeper for AI transaction categorization in small accounting practices. Pricing, ledgers, and when to pick each."
>
  <h1>Booke AI vs Botkeeper</h1>
  <p>Both automate bank feeds and month-end work for firms. Pick by stack depth, price meter, and whether you want software-only or a fuller firm platform.</p>

  <table>
    <thead><tr><th></th><th><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/booke-ai`}>Booke AI</a></th><th><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/tools/botkeeper`}>Botkeeper</a></th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>Best for</td><td>Practices that want AI categorization inside existing QBO/Xero files at a published per-business price</td><td>Firms that want a full bookkeeping platform (close tracker, client hub, firm insights) priced per client license</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Pricing (verified Oct 2026)</td><td>Business $129/business/mo; firm/white-label plans by quote</td><td>Infinite licenses from $149/mo (1–4) down to $59/mo (25+); annual lower; optional human bookkeeping services extra</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ledgers</td><td>Works inside QuickBooks Online and Xero</td><td>Firm platform with bank linking and firm-managed client books (QBO-oriented practice stacks)</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Core AI job</td><td>Daily bank-feed categorization, OCR/doc matching, missing-doc requests, exception review</td><td>AI categorization, auto bank recs, journal entries, autonomous month-end review with anomaly detection</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Firm angle</td><td>Multi-client + white-label available on firm tier; meter is per business</td><td>Built for firms: entity licenses, Activity Hub, Close Tracker, volume discounts as client count grows</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>When to choose Booke AI</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You want a clear published price ($129/business/mo) before talking to sales.</li>
    <li>Clients already live in QuickBooks Online or Xero and should stay there.</li>
    <li>The main pain is daily categorization, document matching, and chasing missing docs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>When to choose Botkeeper</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You need firm-wide close visibility, client collaboration, and a practice platform—not only a categorizer.</li>
    <li>You have (or will have) enough clients for volume license tiers to beat flat per-business pricing.</li>
    <li>You may later add Botkeeper’s human bookkeeping services on top of the software.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>FAQ</h2>
  {faqs.map(([q, a]) => (<><h3>{q}</h3><p>{a}</p></>))}
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={faqLd} />

  <p><a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}/category/categorization`}>All transaction categorization tools</a></p>
</Base>

<style>
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 1rem 0; font-size: 0.95rem; }
  th, td { border: 1px solid #ddd; padding: 0.5rem 0.6rem; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
  th { background: #f6f6f6; }
</style>
